        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "At room temperature, Yb(OAc)3·6H2O (0.2 mmol, 0.084 g), H4L1 (0.2 mmol, 0.076 g) and H2L2 (0.1 mmol, 0.014 g) were dissolved in 9 mL EtOH, then triethylamine in MeOH (1.0 mol L−1, 1 mL) was added. The mixture was heated for 30 min under reflux with stirring, then cooled to room temperature. The clear solution was obtained by filtration and slow diffusion of diethyl ether into the solution for one week gave the red crystalline product of 1. The lanthanide complex was synthesized using a Schlenk system.",
